{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/pulls/519","id":4480932921,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT5mrCM8AAAABCxWcOQ","html_url":"https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/pull/519","diff_url":"https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/pull/519.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/pull/519.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/519","number":519,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(express): v2 hotfix fast lane upgrade (GH-516)","user":{"login":"noelsaw1","id":56978803,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2OTc4ODAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56978803?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1","html_url":"https://github.com/noelsaw1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/noelsaw1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\nUpgrades the `/express` hotfix fast lane (`skills/express/SKILL.md`, `utils/py/express.py`) to v2, addressing operational frictions identified in GH-516:\n- **Branch commit flexibility:** Permits up to 2 local commits on task branches ahead of `origin/development`, computing changes as the union of pre-committed branch diff and working tree modifications/untracked files. Refuses >2 commits (`too-many-commits`) and diverged branches (`task-clone`).\n- **Recovery & resume subcommand:** Implements `express.py resume --issue <N> [--sha <SHA>] [--dry-run]` to safely recover and complete reconciliation if an express run is interrupted after the direct development push.\n- **Subsystem tolerance & dry-run:** Adds `--allow-multi-subsystem` flag and auto-allows micro-diffs (<= 30 insertions across <= 2 files); adds `--dry-run` across all subcommands (`check`, `docs`, `ledger`, `land`, `resume`, `run`).\n- **Central telemetry mirroring:** Mirrors `.tick` event JSONL receipts to `~/.config/xyz/events/` (wrapped in `try...except OSError:`).\n- **Test suite expansion:** Expands `test/gh267-express-skill.sh` with 54 assertions covering all v2 additions and edge cases.\n\n## Plan QA\n- Reviewed and approved via Agy relay (`relay-system/2026-09-08/gh516-express-plan-qa-agy.md`).\n- Active doc: `PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-516-EXPRESS-TRUE-DIRECT-PUSH-PLAN.md`.\n\n## Verification\n- Local test suites verified:\n  - `bash test/gh267-express-skill.sh` -> PASS (54 passed, 0 failed)\n  - `bash test/wave-reconcile.sh` -> PASS (16 passed, 0 failed)\n  - `python3 utils/py/releases_app.py check` -> clean (0 failures)\n  - `utils/pdda/pdda.sh run` -> clean (0 errors)\n  - Full local pre-push gate -> GREEN (in 769s)\n\nCloses #516\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added Express preview mode with `--dry-run`.\n  * Added `resume` recovery for interrupted landings.\n  * Added support for branches with up to two local commits.\n  * Added multi-subsystem support through `--allow-multi-subsystem`, with automatic handling for small changes.\n  * Improved event reporting and reconciliation for Express operations.\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated Express guidance, roadmap tracking, leaderboard entries, and planning materials for the new workflow.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-09-09T03:56:37Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T18:13:56Z","closed_at":"2026-09-09T18:13:53Z","merged_at":"2026-